agent-memory-mcp (0.4.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Read-only web browser for people at /: projects, entries per
    project, each entry rendered from Markdown for reading, and search.
    Same Host allow-list as /mcp; no JavaScript required and no network
    fetches.

 -- April White <claude@sneakyrabbits.io>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:21:08 +0000

agent-memory-mcp (0.3.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New edit tool: change part of an entry with exact-text replacements
    and appends instead of resending the whole body; atomic, and
    concurrent edits re-apply rather than overwrite.
  * get takes a section (Markdown heading) and lists the body headings.
  * remember, edit and update return metadata and body_chars instead of
    echoing the body.

 -- April White <claude@sneakyrabbits.io>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:02:38 +0000

agent-memory-mcp (0.2.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Man page now covers configuration, environment, files and examples
    (help2man --include), checked at build time.
  * Install /etc/default/agent-memory-mcp as 0600, since MONGODB_URI may
    carry credentials.

 -- April White <claude@sneakyrabbits.io>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:08:34 +0000

agent-memory-mcp (0.2.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Log the accepted Host names at startup, and warn when the Host
    allow-list would reject remote clients (they get HTTP 403, which MCP
    clients report as a sign-in failure).
  * Ship the agent-memory plugin for Claude Code and Codex (plugin/,
    versioned to match).
  * CI: Node 24 actions, pinned ubuntu-24.04 runner.

